Spec: specs/001-core-and-anthropic-passthrough/spec.md (AC2, AC36, AC37, AC38, AC39)
Why this approach: registered() returns the one adapter list and one profile list; upstreamSpecs derives config.Options.Upstreams from each adapter's Name and DefaultBaseURL, and the same list feeds AddAdapter with cfg.Upstreams[a.Name()], so a config key and its adapter cannot drift. registry.Mount goes first in the server.New mounts, then deps.mount. cmd/gateway stays the only non-test importer of an adapter or a profile.
Alternatives rejected: keeping the interim hard-coded UpstreamSpec (a second copy of the name and default URL); a package-level var for the lists (mutable global shared across tests).
Trade-off / known limit: TestProxy_SecretsNotLogged swaps os.Stderr, so it is not parallel; it runs two gateways (live and dead upstream) because one adapter has one upstream.
Verified by: TestRun_ProxiesAnthropicEndToEnd (claude-code / api_key and unknown / none lines, upstream sees prefix-stripped paths and ?beta=true), TestRun_UpstreamEnvOverrideLogged (passed on arrival via the interim list; proved by passing nil upstream specs and watching it fail, then reverting), TestProxy_SecretsNotLogged (success, 502, mid-stream abort with upstream_aborted, panicking route; sentinel absent from stdout and stderr); the first two failed with 404 before the mount; go test -race -count=2 ./cmd/gateway; make verify.
